/* The site questions sloth answers when no --questions file is given
 * (#244). Not a header: no include guard, on purpose. Every includer
 * defines X(QID, PRIORITY, TEXT, DECISION) first and gets one expansion
 * per row.
 *
 *   QID       Q1 .. Q7: the question's id, as the question_status record
 *             and the question_status table write it.
 *   PRIORITY  1 is the most urgent; --notify-priority N notifies on the
 *             questions of priority N and lower numbers.
 *   TEXT      one question in plain words (FM 2-0 (2004) 1-34: a
 *             priority question asks only one question).
 *   DECISION  the operator's decision the answer supports (1-34: it
 *             supports a decision).
 *
 * Which alert kinds are each question's indicators is
 * include/sloth_question_map.def; docs/wiki/site-questions.md has the
 * judgement behind both. Change them there and here together. */
X(Q1, 1, "Is a device impersonating one of my networks?",
         "Warn users off the network and find the transmitter.")
X(Q2, 1, "Is a device that I do not know on my network?",
         "Remove the device and change the network key.")
X(Q3, 1, "Is a device collecting key material near my site?",
         "Change the network key or the credentials now.")
X(Q4, 2, "Is a device or a person surveying my site again and again?",
         "Raise the watch on the site and keep the evidence.")
X(Q5, 3, "Is my site revealing information?",
         "Change the settings or devices that disclose the site.")
X(Q6, 2, "Is the radio environment being denied or degraded?",
         "Move channel or band, or find the source.")
X(Q7, 1, "Is the sensor able to see what it must see?",
         "Trust the other answers, or fix the sensor first.")
